// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-13 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1087.002
// Description: Detects active directory enumeration activity using known AdFind CLI flags
// False positives:
//   - Authorized administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://www.joeware.net/freetools/tools/adfind/
//   - https://social.technet.microsoft.com/wiki/contents/articles/7535.adfind-command-examples.aspx
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1087.002/T1087.002.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ebd26c2d9cd57dc9489faa1f1346577be9947747/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_adfind_enumeration.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "lockoutduration" or ProcessCommandLine contains "lockoutthreshold" or ProcessCommandLine contains "lockoutobservationwindow" or ProcessCommandLine contains "maxpwdage" or ProcessCommandLine contains "minpwdage" or ProcessCommandLine contains "minpwdlength" or ProcessCommandLine contains "pwdhistorylength" or ProcessCommandLine contains "pwdproperties") or ProcessCommandLine contains "-sc admincountdmp" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-sc exchaddresses"
